// `yo check --test-bodies` on a test body that auto-boxes a closure for a
// `Dyn` (no explicit `box`). The synthesized `rc(...)` call was built with
// node id 0, shared by every other such node, so the ExprInfo side table (keyed
// by id) answered the callee atom with another node's entry: "box is not
// callable: it has type unit".
// issues/fixed/an-auto-boxed-dyn-value-builds-its-box-call-with-node-id-zero.md
// The closure writes its implicit capture, so it is `FnMut` (in an `Fn`
// closure the write is E0913, #1932), and a `Dyn(FnMut(...))` call borrows the
// closure exclusively, so the binding is `mut`.
{ assert } :: import("std/assert");
test("an auto-boxed closure in a test body", {
  mut(x) := 1;
  (mut(closure) : Dyn(FnMut(y : i32) -> i32)) = dyn(y => {
    x = (x + y);
    return(x);
  });
  assert(closure(1) == 2, "called");
});
